-## What it cannot do yet
+## Importing media and exporting video
 
-The MCP tools cannot import media files or export video yet. Add images, video, and audio through the [normal multimedia UI](./working-with-multimedia.md), and use [Exporting Your Project](../tutorial-basics/exporting-your-project.md) when you're ready to render the finished video.
+Ask the agent to use `add_media` with an absolute filesystem path, for example:
+
+```json
+{"path": "/home/me/Pictures/diagram.png"}
+```
+
+The file must be on the machine running AniMathIO. The tool adds it to the media resources, selects the matching resource panel, and waits for it to mount and decode before adding timeline elements. Common image formats, MP4/WebM/MOV/M4V video, and MP3/WAV/OGG/M4A/AAC/FLAC audio are accepted by extension; actual decoding depends on the codecs available in Electron. Missing files, unsupported types, mounting timeouts, and decoding failures report an error. You can still use the [normal multimedia UI](./working-with-multimedia.md) to manage resources.
+
+To render the finished project, ask the agent to use `export_video`, for example:
+
+```json
+{"path": "/home/me/Videos/explanation.webm", "format": "webm"}
+```
+
+The destination must be an absolute path ending in `.mp4` or `.webm`. If you omit `format`, the extension determines it; if supplied, it must match the extension. The parent directory must already exist, and an existing destination file is overwritten. This exports directly to that path instead of triggering a browser download. Use `save_project` separately to save an editable project.
+
+**Export takes at least as long as the video is long.** A 30-second project records for 30 seconds, then needs additional time for conversion and writing. MP4 conversion fetches the FFmpeg core if needed and adds processing time; WebM avoids that conversion. Configure a generous timeout in your MCP client, keep AniMathIO and the project open, and avoid editing the scene or changing playback during export. A second export is rejected while one is in progress. The tool reports success only after the destination file is written, and reports recording, conversion, or writing errors to the agent.
+
+See [Exporting Your Project](../tutorial-basics/exporting-your-project.md) for the normal export UI.
 
